{%- comment -%}
  AJ About — the page IS the monitor.

  THE SCREEN IS THE VIEWPORT, not an object drawn inside it. Everything between
  the header and the footer is one dark, scanlined, phosphor-lit surface, and
  the story is a terminal session running on it. That reading solves every
  problem the earlier versions had, by removing the thing causing them:

    - A PHOTOGRAPHED monitor has a screen that is a fixed region of a raster.
      It cannot grow, so long copy either shrank or overflowed the bezel.
    - A DRAWN monitor grew fine, but a bezel around a page-length story is a
      picture frame: it forced a tall narrow column and never fit on a screen.

  A full-bleed screen has neither failure mode. There is no bezel to overflow
  and no shape to preserve, so the copy just reflows, which is what copy does.

  MOBILE IS THE SAME IDEA, NOT A REDUCED ONE. No breakpoint hides the effect,
  because there is no chrome left to hide — and a phone is already a rectangle
  of glass, so a full-bleed CRT is arguably more convincing there than on a
  desktop. It only tightens: narrower gutters, larger type against the shorter
  measure, and a coarser scanline pitch (see the note in the media query — 3px
  on a 3x display is sub-pixel mush).

  THE EYEBROW IS THE COMMAND LINE NOW. "About us" in purple above a terminal
  was the last thing on this page still behaving like a normal website. It is
  the prompt that opens the session instead, and it reads "Our story" because
  that is what the footer link promises.

  THE h1 IS STILL A REAL HEADING. The prompt characters are decorative and
  aria-hidden, so the accessible name is "Our story" and not "C colon backslash
  greater-than OUR STORY". Search and screen readers get an ordinary heading;
  everyone else sees a command.

  NOTHING HERE USES THE BRAND YELLOW. The palette on a lit screen is phosphor
  and the soft white it throws. Dropping #ffe000 in would read as a web page
  wearing a terminal costume — and the yellow is doing its job everywhere else
  on the site, which is what makes it mean something there.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
-%}

<div
  class="aj-crt-page"
  style="--aj-crt-phosphor: {{ s.phosphor }}; --aj-crt-screen: {{ s.screen_color }};"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    STATUS BARS, and they exist because of a measurement. At 1920px the reading
    column is 513px, which leaves 703px of dead screen on EACH side — 73% of
    the surface doing nothing. Widening the measure was not the answer: 63
    characters a line is already correct and stretching it would trade a
    cosmetic problem for a legibility one.

    So the width gets used instead of filled. Every DOS editor and file manager
    ever written framed its work area in full-width bars, which is precisely
    why they read as an APPLICATION rather than as text on a background — and
    it turns the empty sides into the app's own chrome rather than into void.

    Decorative, so both are hidden from assistive tech.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.bar_left != blank or s.bar_right != blank -%}
    <div class="aj-crt-page__bar aj-crt-page__bar--top" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>{{ s.bar_left }}</span>
      <span class="aj-crt-page__bar-mid">{{ s.bar_mid }}</span>
      <span>{{ s.bar_right }}</span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div
    class="aj-crt-page__inner"
    style="padding-block-start: {{ s.padding-block-start }}px; padding-block-end: {{ s.padding-block-end }}px;"
  >
    {%- if s.boot_lines != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        aria-hidden: atmosphere, not content. A screen reader announcing
        "greater-than LOADING ORIGIN dot TXT" ahead of the story is noise.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="aj-crt-page__boot" data-aj-boot aria-hidden="true">
        {%- assign lines = s.boot_lines | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
        {%- for line in lines -%}
          {%- assign trimmed = line | strip -%}
          {%- if trimmed != blank -%}
            <p class="aj-crt-page__bootline">{{ trimmed | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
      <h1 class="aj-crt-page__cmd">
        <span class="aj-crt-page__prompt" aria-hidden="true">{{ s.prompt | default: 'C:\>' }}</span>
        {{- s.heading | escape -}}
      </h1>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.lead != blank -%}
      <div class="aj-crt-page__lead rte">{{ s.lead }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.cmd_1 != blank -%}
      <p class="aj-crt-page__step" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="aj-crt-page__prompt">{{ s.prompt | default: 'C:\>' }}</span>
        {{- s.cmd_1 | escape -}}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.body_1 != blank -%}
      <div class="aj-crt-page__body rte">{{ s.body_1 }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.pull_quote != blank -%}
      <p class="aj-crt-page__pull">{{ s.pull_quote | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.cmd_2 != blank -%}
      <p class="aj-crt-page__step" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="aj-crt-page__prompt">{{ s.prompt | default: 'C:\>' }}</span>
        {{- s.cmd_2 | escape -}}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.body_2 != blank -%}
      <div class="aj-crt-page__body rte">{{ s.body_2 }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.cmd_3 != blank -%}
      <p class="aj-crt-page__step" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="aj-crt-page__prompt">{{ s.prompt | default: 'C:\>' }}</span>
        {{- s.cmd_3 | escape -}}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.signoff != blank -%}
      <p class="aj-crt-page__signoff">{{ s.signoff | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.tagline != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Ruled, not filled. A solid colour block is the one thing that looks
        pasted onto a lit screen; a box drawn in rules is what a terminal
        actually does to make you look at something.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="aj-crt-page__tagline">{{ s.tagline | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.primary_text != blank or s.secondary_text != blank -%}
      <div class="aj-crt-page__actions">
        {%- if s.primary_text != blank -%}
          <a class="aj-crt-page__btn" href="{{ s.primary_link | default: '/' }}">
            <span class="aj-crt-page__prompt" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
            {{- s.primary_text | escape -}}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.secondary_text != blank -%}
          <a class="aj-crt-page__btn" href="{{ s.secondary_link | default: '/' }}">
            <span class="aj-crt-page__prompt" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
            {{- s.secondary_text | escape -}}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} The session is still open. {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="aj-crt-page__caret" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="aj-crt-page__prompt">{{ s.prompt | default: 'C:\>' }}</span>
      <span class="aj-crt-page__cursor"></span>
    </p>
  </div>

  {%- if s.bar_footer != blank -%}
    <div class="aj-crt-page__bar aj-crt-page__bar--bottom" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>{{ s.bar_footer }}</span>
      <span>{{ s.bar_footer_right }}</span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

<script>
  (function () {
    var script = document.currentScript;
    if (!script) return;
    var root = script.parentElement;
    var boot = root && root.querySelector('[data-aj-boot]');
    if (!boot) return;

    /* Reduced motion gets the finished state, not a slower one. The lines are
       already in the DOM and already visible; this only opts IN to the
       sequence, so doing nothing here is the correct fallback for
       reduced-motion AND for JS being unavailable. */
    var reduce = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
    if (reduce && reduce.matches) return;

    var lines = boot.querySelectorAll('.aj-crt-page__bootline');
    for (var i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
      lines[i].style.animationDelay = i * 0.4 + 's';
    }
    boot.setAttribute('data-aj-boot', 'running');
  })();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    FULL BLEED, escaping whatever container the page template wraps this in.
    `100vw` with a `calc(50% - 50vw)` margin is the reliable way to do that
    without knowing the container's width. max-width: 100% is the guard: on a
    desktop with a classic scrollbar, 100vw is WIDER than the document, and
    without it the page gains a horizontal scroll.
  */
  .aj-crt-page {
    --aj-crt-phosphor: #5cf08a;
    --aj-crt-screen: #0b100c;
    --aj-crt-text: #d6f5e0;
    --aj-crt-dim: rgb(214 245 224 / 0.74);

    position: relative;
    width: 100vw;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin-inline: calc(50% - 50vw);
    color: var(--aj-crt-text);

    background-color: var(--aj-crt-screen);
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.035) 0 1px,
      transparent 1px 3px
    );

    /* A tube falls off toward its edges. On a full-bleed surface this is the
       difference between "a section with a dark background" and glass. */
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 240px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.75),
      inset 0 0 60px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.45);
  }

  /* The bloom pooling in the middle of the tube. A pseudo element so it sits
     above the scanlines and below every word. */
  .aj-crt-page::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse 70% 55% at 50% 45%,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 7%, transparent) 0%,
      transparent 70%
    );
  }

  /* Inverse of the screen: solid phosphor with the screen colour punched out
     of it, which is exactly how a DOS status line was drawn. */
  .aj-crt-page__bar {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    color: var(--aj-crt-screen);
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__bar-mid {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    /* The middle cell is the first thing to go — three cells in 390px is three
       cramped ones. */
    .aj-crt-page__bar-mid {
      display: none;
    }

    .aj-crt-page__bar {
      padding-inline: 1rem;
      font-size: 0.625rem;
    }
  }

  .aj-crt-page__inner {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 64ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 2rem;
  }

  /* ---- the session ------------------------------------------------------ */

  .aj-crt-page__boot {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__bootline,
  .aj-crt-page__cmd,
  .aj-crt-page__step,
  .aj-crt-page__pull,
  .aj-crt-page__signoff,
  .aj-crt-page__tagline,
  .aj-crt-page__btn,
  .aj-crt-page__caret {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);

    /* Bloom plus a half-pixel of RGB fringing. A shadow mask never converged
       perfectly, so phosphor text always carried a faint red edge one side and
       blue the other — it is the single cheapest thing that separates "green
       text" from "a CRT". Half a pixel at low alpha, because any more and the
       pixel face starts to look out of focus rather than analogue. */
    text-shadow:
      0 0 14px color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 45%, transparent),
      -0.5px 0 0 rgb(255 60 90 / 0.28),
      0.5px 0 0 rgb(70 190 255 / 0.28);
  }

  .aj-crt-page__bootline {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  /* Default state is VISIBLE — the animation is opted into by script, so both
     no-JS and reduced-motion land on a finished screen rather than a blank one. */
  [data-aj-boot='running'] .aj-crt-page__bootline {
    opacity: 0;
    animation: aj-crt-print 0.01s linear forwards;
  }

  @keyframes aj-crt-print {
    to {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  /* The h1, set as the command that opened the session. */
  .aj-crt-page__cmd {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__prompt {
    margin-inline-end: 0.6em;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /*
    The commands between sections. Deliberately QUIETER than the h1 — they are
    punctuation, not headings, and at the same weight they would compete with
    the one line on the page that is a real heading.

    aria-hidden, and that is a decision rather than an oversight. "TYPE
    HOW-IT-STARTED.TXT" is not a section title anybody needs read aloud, and
    promoting them to real h2s would put four fake headings in the document
    outline of what is one continuous story.
  */
  .aj-crt-page__step {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  /* Archivo for the story. Ohpixel is a pixel grid and loses it in sentences —
     aj-brand.css says so, and five hundred words would prove it. */
  .aj-crt-page__lead p {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    font-size: 1.3125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--aj-crt-text);
  }

  /*
    1.0625rem, not the theme's inherited 14px. On white at full black, 14px is
    fine; here it is dimmed text on a near-black screen, and the same size that
    reads as compact on a light page reads as squinting on a dark one. The dim
    is lifted with it for the same reason.
  */
  .aj-crt-page__body p {
    margin: 0 0 1.3rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--aj-crt-dim);
  }

  .aj-crt-page__body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__pull {
    margin: 2.25rem 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 0 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__signoff {
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__tagline {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 45%, transparent);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__btn {
    flex: 1 1 14rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 55%, transparent);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .aj-crt-page__btn:hover {
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 14%, transparent);
    }
  }

  .aj-crt-page__caret {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .aj-crt-page__cursor {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.55em;
    height: 1em;
    background: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    vertical-align: -0.12em;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 55%, transparent);
    animation: aj-crt-blink 1.1s steps(1, end) infinite;
  }

  @keyframes aj-crt-blink {
    50% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  /* ---- mobile ------------------------------------------------------------ */

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .aj-crt-page__inner {
      padding-inline: 1.25rem;
    }

    /*
      A 3px scanline pitch on a 3x phone display is sub-pixel mush — it reads
      as grain rather than as lines. Opening it to 4px keeps them legible as
      scanlines at the density a phone actually renders, and the vignette comes
      in because 240px of inset shadow on a 390px-wide screen would swallow
      the middle of the page.
    */
    .aj-crt-page {
      background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(
        to bottom,
        rgb(255 255 255 / 0.04) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 4px
      );
      box-shadow:
        inset 0 0 120px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.7),
        inset 0 0 40px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4);
    }

    .aj-crt-page__cmd {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
    }

    .aj-crt-page__lead p {
      font-size: 1.0625rem;
    }

    /* Ohpixel comes down harder than the body face: a pixel grid landing
       between whole pixels is where it starts to look broken. */
    .aj-crt-page__pull {
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    }

    .aj-crt-page__tagline {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }

    /* Full width — two half-width buttons on a phone are two small buttons. */
    .aj-crt-page__btn {
      flex-basis: 100%;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .aj-crt-page__bootline,
    .aj-crt-page__cursor {
      animation: none !important;
      opacity: 1 !important;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ About",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The whole page is the screen. Founders stay anonymous — 'two coworkers', no names, no photos."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Status bars" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_left", "label": "Top bar — left", "default": "The Yoink Co." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_mid", "label": "Top bar — middle", "default": "our-story.txt" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_right", "label": "Top bar — right", "default": "Read only" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_footer", "label": "Bottom bar — left", "default": "Esc = back to the shop" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_footer_right", "label": "Bottom bar — right", "default": "One deal a day" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Terminal" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "prompt", "label": "Prompt", "default": "C:\\>" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "boot_lines",
      "label": "Boot sequence",
      "info": "One line each. Prints line by line on load. Uppercased automatically — keep them short.",
      "default": "The Yoink Co. Terminal v1.0\n> 640K OK\n> Mounting c:\\yoink ...\n> Loading origin.txt ...\n> OK"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Command / page heading",
      "info": "Renders after the prompt as the h1. This is the page's real heading, so keep it meaningful.",
      "default": "Our story"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Story" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The commands below print between sections as C:\\> lines. They are atmosphere, not headings — leave one blank to skip it."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "lead",
      "label": "Opening paragraph",
      "default": "<p>We're a couple of '90s kids. We missed the dot-com boom by about a decade, came of age dodging recessions and pandemics, and have basically spent our whole adult lives being told the timing's bad. So instead of waiting around for a better hand, we decided to have some fun with the one we've got.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cmd_1", "label": "Command before section 2", "default": "type how-it-started.txt" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body_1",
      "label": "Body — before the pull quote",
      "default": "<p>The short version: two guys that had a lot of fun working together, until one of them decided to move off. So, in order to keep the bromance alive, we did the most reasonable thing two grown adults could do.</p><p>We started an online store.</p><p>The Yoink is our excuse to keep hanging out, keep scheming, and finally have some fun with retail — because the places we came from were about as playful as a tax form. Case in point: one of us stayed up half the night last week, wide awake, brain fully hijacked by what should tomorrow's deal be. That's not a healthy relationship with a website. We're aware. We're not stopping.</p><p>Here's the bit: every single day, we go dig up one genuinely cool, slightly random, actually-worth-owning thing — and drop it at a price that feels a little bit illegal.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pull_quote",
      "label": "Pull quote",
      "info": "Set in the pixel face and uppercased. Keep it short — it loses its grid in long sentences.",
      "default": "One deal. One day. Blink and it's someone else's."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cmd_2", "label": "Command before section 3", "default": "type the-bit.txt" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body_2",
      "label": "Body — after the pull quote",
      "default": "<p>We call it the Yoink of the Day, because yoink is the sound of grabbing something great half a second before the person next to you.</p><p>Nature's already full of professionals at this. Raccoons yoink the dog food. Seagulls yoink the fries. Bears yoink the whole picnic basket and don't even say thank you. We're just doing it with better taste and free-ish shipping — a little retail Robin Hood move where somehow everybody wins: you get the score, the good stuff finds its people, and we get to keep the lights on.</p><p>To be clear, we are not out here trying to buy a yacht. A canoe, maybe. We're just making the most of the hand we've been dealt — and, conveniently, dealing is kind of our whole thing. Mostly we like tracking down cool stuff for cheap and handing you the deal like it's a dare. Some days the Yoink is exactly what you didn't know you needed. Some days it's a penguin-shaped thing that is very much Not For You — no notes, there's a new one tomorrow.</p><p>So stick around. Watch the drops. Rummage the Bargain Bin between yoinks. And when the good one hits — you know what to do.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cmd_3", "label": "Command before sign-off", "default": "echo %welcome%" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "signoff",
      "label": "Sign-off",
      "default": "Welcome to The Yoink. Yoink accordingly."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Close" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tagline",
      "label": "Tagline box",
      "default": "One deal a day. Yoink it before it's gone."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "primary_text", "label": "First link", "default": "See today's Yoink" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "primary_link", "label": "First link URL" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "secondary_text", "label": "Second link", "default": "Dig through the Bargain Bin" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "secondary_link", "label": "Second link URL" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "phosphor", "label": "Phosphor", "default": "#5cf08a" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "screen_color", "label": "Screen", "default": "#0b100c" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 72 },
